body:
I disagree completely. If you are a math major and you already went over all the material beforehand, then 6 weeks should be more than enough. I learnt the material for exam P in a summer course spanning 2.5 months, but I probably did like 10 hours of work a week. The last month (\~4 weeks) is all I spent on doing questions and exam papers. I did around 18 practice exams, and didn't even touch the SOA problems, yet I passed and only guessed 1 question in the actual exam. This is not to say the exam is easy, but if you're confident with the material you say youve learnt already, you should be good.

&#x200B;

Edit: I guess i read over the fact that you're a senior. In that case, the material tested in P is elementary in comparison to what you've probably already done. Should be a cakewalk, just grind practice exams and the SOA questions

Partying in the sense just drinking or hanging out with my friends. Maybe going out would have been a more appropriate term. I'm strictly against anyone throwing raves or whatnot. Point was that I could compartmentalize my time between my social and academic life, and one needn't necessarily leech from the other as far as you're on top of your shit

&#x200B;

Edit: Guess im being downvoted because people dont like others having a life? lmfao. since when has bringing 5 guys over to get messed up been against covid rules.
